new leaks and rumors about the 9th  generation budget ipad have started to  emerge online  and based on what i'm seeing from these  leaks i personally believe  that a lot of people are totally wrong  so what i'm going to do in this video  is explain the specs and features that  are most likely to come  on the new ipad based on apple's past  release  trends and just simple common sense  so before we get into that let me show  you all of those leaks  back in november ipad 9 rumors started  by triple zero leaker on twitter  claiming that ming chakuo expects a new  ipad 9  to be released in the second half of  2021  with an updated design then in december  a report  from chinese website cn beta claimed  that the ipad 9 would come  with an a13 chip 4 gigs of ram  64 gigs of base storage and a 10.5 inch  display  with a starting price of 299 dollars  which is even lower than the current  model and then finally  just a couple of days ago mac otakara  claimed that the new ipad will feature a  thinner  lighter design with a touch id home  button and a lightning port  but they expect the display size to  remain the same  10.2 inches so that's basically all that  we've got in terms of leaks  and as you can tell they're all  conflicting with each other  in one way or another and i personally  think a lot of those details  are totally wrong let me explain the  first way i want to attack those rumors  is by looking at what apple's done  with the budget ipad in the past apple's  fifth generation ipad came  with the old 9.7 inch display with a  home button  and a non-laminated display then with  the ipad 6  apple upgraded it with an a10 chip and  apple pencil support but they kept the  same  9.7 inch display the year after that the  ipad 7 kept  the same exact a10 chip but they added  the smart connector  and changed the design to feature a new  10.2 inch display and then just a few  months ago  apple released the ipad 8 and the only  difference  was the upgraded a12 chip that's  literally  the only change so from all of that  there are a couple of different things  that we can learn  number one is that apple has been  updating their budget ipad  every single year and two apple has been  extremely conservative  with their year over year upgrades and  if you look at the trends from the past  few ipads  apple seems to have it on a tick-tock  upgrade cycle  one year they upgrade the design without  changing the chip  and the next year they upgrade the chip  without changing the design  so if we assume that apple will continue  with this trend  then we can expect that the ipad 9  coming sometime this year  will most likely stick to the same a12  bionic chip not the a13 like many of  those leakers  are claiming and keep in mind that for a  budget ipad  the a12 is definitely powerful enough so  that means that if apple is not  upgrading the chip this year then the  likely upgrade the design so let's talk  about what apple can do with that  if we look at the history of the budget  ipad it was always taking  hand-me-downs from the more expensive  ipads  in terms of technology for example it  was the last  larger sized ipad to get the smart  connector and it still has  a cheap non-laminated display without p3  wide color gamut support  it still doesn't have an anti-reflective  coating  it still has the most outdated a12 chip  and it still features  a horrible 1.2 megapixel selfie camera  and of course all of that makes sense  because this is the budget ipad that  we're talking about  priced at only 329 so based on that  logic  we can expect the budget ipad line to be  the very last  to get updated with a new edge to edge  display design  as we've already seen apple do with the  ipad pro  and the ipad air 4. so based on what  apple has done in the past  the new ipad 9 will likely stick to the  older  home button design for at least one more  year and since they just updated the  chip  last year apple will probably update the  design  this year so the big question is this  if they're not gonna give it the full  flat back redesign  what exactly is gonna change in my  personal opinion  it makes the most sense to give the ipad  9 the same exact body  and 10.5 inch display as the ipad air  3. this is the absolute easiest route  for apple to take  since they already have all of the  tooling and the internals  ready to go and as we already know the  ipad air 4 uses a totally new design  based on the ipad pro so apple can  simply take  the ipad air 3 and change nothing at all  except for giving it a weaker a12 chip  and  boom there you go that's the new ipad 9.  it's going to be just good enough to  make it worth it since the biggest  downside of the ipad 8  is the non-laminated display that really  sucks  compared to the rest of the lineup as  well as the horrible  selfie camera giving the ipad 9 the same  design as the air 3  will fix both of those issues and it's  going to be easy on  apple since it'll support the same  keyboard cases  that the ipad air 3 supported this is  the path of least resistance  so i personally expect apple to go this  route  this would also mean that the touch id  home button is staying  the lightning port is staying and the  first gen apple pencil support  is staying now in terms of the specs and  the price i personally expect the ipad 9  to get the same  three gigs of ram with that a12 chip  i expect the storage to stick with the  same 32 gigabytes at the base  price which you might disagree with but  if you think about it  the new ipad air 4 comes with 64 gigs  and it costs  600 apple giving the budget ipad  64 gigs of storage would be really  shocking  since i personally expect the price to  stick to the same 329  which goes against those other rumors  that we talked about  which claimed apple would lower the  price to 299  i completely disagree with them because  i personally believe  that apple is attempting to raise the  price of their entire ipad lineup  they did it with the redesigned ipad pro  in 2018.  they did it with the redesigned ipad air  4 just a few months ago  so to me it makes the most sense to keep  the price of the budget ipad  at the same 329 until  they finally give the ipad the modern  flat back  inside full redesign with support for  the 2nd gen apple pencil  which will be enough for apple to  justify raising the price  to 399 now out of all of the  speculations that i just made  there is only one thing that i'm unsure  about  whether apple intends to give the ipad  the full  redesign next year or two years from now  if you think about it two years sounds  like a very long time for it to stick  with the old design  but then apple would be staying true to  their tick-tock  upgrade cycle of new design and then new  chip this would mean that next year's  ipad would get the a14  chip with no other major changes and  then two years from now  it would finally get a full redesign but  stick to the same a14 chip but then  on the other hand what if apple is  planning to give it the full redesign  next year so they can raise the base  price  this would mean that they would be  giving the ipad a new design  two years in a row which would be  breaking the cycle  since they would also need to update the  chip at some point  as well so here's my theory for option  number two  what if apple quite literally takes the  ipad air 3  with its a13 bionic chip and 4 gigabytes  of ram  and simply rebrands it as the ipad 9.  this would by far be the easiest route  to take  and it would allow them to fully  redesign the ipad  next year while keeping the same a13  chip  on that new model those are the two  options and as  of right now i'm not really sure which  one apple is going to go with  but with all of that said the only  remaining question  is when the ipad 9 is going to be  released so let's quickly answer that  for the past few years  apple's budget ipads have been released  in either september  or march with the most recent ipad 8  being released in september and recent  leaks are pointing to both the ipad pro  and the ipad mini 6 to get released this  upcoming march so in my personal opinion  it doesn't make sense to release three  out of the four ipad models  all at the same time in march so we can  safely assume  that the ipad 9 is probably coming this  september  or at the very least sometime this fall  so to finish off this video  here's a full spec list of what i expect  for the 2021 ipad 9 so you can  screenshot this  if you'd like to share this with others  now if you totally disagree with me  go ahead and comment your thoughts down  below but if you enjoyed it  click that circle above to subscribe and  definitely watch those ipad league  videos  right over there thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next one  you

